{%- comment -%}
  Theme-editor text that also follows the storefront language.

  Editor settings hold one value for every language, so on its own a setting
  shows the same (English) text on /zh. This keeps the editor in charge of the
  primary language and swaps in the locale translation everywhere else:

    - primary language → the editor value, exactly as entered
    - other languages  → the translation at `key` (Edit default theme content)
    - editor value blank → nothing, in every language (blank still hides it),
      unless `fallback` is true, which shows the translation instead

  Accepts:
    value    - REQUIRED. The section/block setting.
    key      - REQUIRED. Locale key holding the translated text.
    fallback - optional. Show the translation when the setting is blank.

  Usage:
    capture heading
      render 'editor-text', value: section.settings.heading, key: 'contact.heading'
    endcapture
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if value == blank
    if fallback
      echo key | t
    endif
  elsif request.locale.primary
    echo value
  else
    echo key | t
  endif
-%}
